ratic method and talk to  us about that so what what in what way  does teaching the Socratic method in  your mind help to prepare  prisoners for when they're out in the  real world to avoid falling into the  same patterns right well with the  Socratic method does is it teaches you  to pause and to reflect on an ideology  or a belief or just a definition of any  of something or just anything something  somebody tells you what the Socratic  method does is it gives you a toolset  so you analyze that whatever you know  you've been told to see if that is  indeed correct or if you agree with it  and you know we find everybody me you  even we we do this you know people just  hand down facts to us people in  authority usually politicians or a boss  or a parent will just tell us something  and we'll just not question it and  assume it's correct and uh so yeah so  that's what the Socratic method does if  you apply it is it helps you to reflect  and to self-analyze and self self  inquiry into into the truth to see if  you agree with yourself and and  essentially you're just living your life  day to day for yourself and you're  believing and acting in in a way that  you agree with and you're not doing  things just because somebody told you  and if people want to learn more about  save by reason where's the best place  for them to do that they can go on our  website say by reason org or they can  follow us on Twitter say by reason all  right I'll tell everybody once again  we've been speaking with Joshua Turner  he is president and founder of the  secular prison outreach organization  saved by reason thanks so much for  telling us your story right on thanks  David it's great to be here man  appreciate it
 

